< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/tacplus/issues/312#issuecomment-6746219993 [2026-11-09T17:03:34Z] checkpoint of #312 (a step) pushed to looper/tacplus-312:  50 files changed, 982 insertions(+), 246 deletions(-)
The fix for #312 is committed (8404f2a5) and queued to land, but it hadn't landed when my time ran out. `just consumer-build` also failed, apparently for an unrelated reason, so I left the issue open; the next run picks up from my last checkpoint.

**What changed:**
- **Pins raised:** every one of the 32 `dependencies.yaml` copies (`example/proto` included) now pins axios ^1.20.0, js-yaml ^4.3.2, zod ^4.6.6, rustls 0.23.46, tokio 1.51.6, webpki-roots 0.26.11, anyhow 1.0.103 and jsonwebtoken 10.3.0. The Cargo.toml files the cross-test scripts write for their own harnesses also had tokio 1.49.0; they now use 1.51.6.
- **x/crypto goes past what the issue recommended:** the five fixtures and eight harness go.mod files now pin `v0.58.1-0.20261009181718-2f1f834330b2` instead of `v0.58.0`. OSV now reports GO-2026-5932 (the unmaintained openpgp package) against v0.58.0, and only this untagged commit fixes it. Nothing generated imports openpgp. I noted in PROPOSALS.md to move back to a tag once v0.59.0 exists.
- **Tests:** a new `scripts/dependency_floor_test.go`, plus an x/crypto floor in `scripts/go_dependency_floor_test.go`. Both failed on the old pins before I raised them, and now refuse any lower pin.
- **OSV:** every distinct pin of the nine packages comes back with no advisory.

**Gates:**
- **`just gates`:** passes locally on the fix, all 16 gates ending `=== OVERALL fail=0 ===`. That includes jwk-alg building the generated TypeScript (`165 cases, 11 accepted`).
- **`just consumer-build`:** failed with exit 1. It stopped while generating the fixture's Python client, on an MCP annotation check (`ContractApi owns MCP tools but is being generated for language "python"`). This change touches no proto, MCP check or Python pin, so I believe main already fails this way, but I didn't have time to confirm on origin/main. Only its Go builds ran; its TypeScript and Rust builds did not.

**Release:** main has taken a feature since v2.6.1 (#321), so main gets no tag. I opened backport pull requests #483–#489 against release/2.0 through release/2.6, which name the patches to cut on merge: v2.0.23, v2.1.17, v2.2.14, v2.3.16, v2.4.16, v2.5.17 and v2.6.6. On those branches I only ran the floor tests (they pass), not the full gates.

**Trace rule:** this change touches no handlers. `looper-trace check` flags only handlers outside this change, and those findings are already filed as #311 and #310.

**Left for the next run:**
1. Confirm the land's verdict.
2. Run `just consumer-build` on origin/main. If it fails the same way, file it as a bug, then run `just consumer-build-typescript`, `-rust` and `-go` on the fix.
3. Post the final comment and close #312.

